step-ca on FenrirOS
===================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled and no CA, key, password or
provisioner exists.

1. Create the CA (needs the step-cli package), as root:
       export STEPPATH=/etc/step-ca
       step ca init --name "My CA" --dns ca.example.org --address :443 \
           --provisioner admin@example.org --password-file /etc/step-ca/password.txt
   (write the password file first, mode 0640, owner root:step-ca; the
   database, if you use one, lives under /var/lib/step-ca, see ca.json "db").
   Make /etc/step-ca/{certs,secrets,config,db} readable by the step-ca group.
2. Optional /etc/step-ca/env: environment for the service (STEPPATH=/etc/step-ca).
3. dinitctl enable step-ca

The service may bind ports below 1024 (cap_net_bind_service). Hardware keys
(YubiKey, PKCS#11 modules, TPM) are supported by this build; the modules
themselves come from their own packages.
